<title>UK: Granada year profits jump 37 percent.</title>
<headline>Granada year profits jump 37 percent.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-11-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year to September 30</p>
<p>			   (million stg unless stated)</p>
<p> Shr (pence)		42.3		   vs 8.0 percent rise</p>
<p> Pretax pre-excepts     480		    vs 37 percent rise</p>
<p> Turnover		   3.82 billion	 vs 60 percent rise</p>
<p>NOTE - Analysts' forecasts on pre-tax profits were in a range of 451 to 468 million stg. Full results breakdown was not immediately available.  </p>
<p> Final dividend (pence) 8.765		  vs 7.9</p>
<p> Total dividend (pence) 13		     vs 11.75</p>
<p> Operating result	 676.9		  vs 388.1</p>
<p> Exceptional cost	  75.6		  vs n/a</p>
<p> Interest paid	    196.5		  vs 36.8</p>
<p> Tax			  108.3		  vs 98.5</p>
<p> Net taxed		  296.5		  vs 252.8</p>
<p> Minority charge	    2.1		  vs 0.2</p>
<p> Attributable	     294.4		  vs 252.6</p>
<p> Pay date		   April 1, 1997</p>
<p> Div registration date  January 14, 1997</p>
<p> Ex-div date		January 6, 1997</p>
<p>NOTE - The exceptional cost relates largely to the acquisition of Forte in January by media and leisure group Granada. -- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
</text>
